WDQSQLever <p>16 Oct 2026, 10:05:18 UTC·Success·1.77 s·496 bytes</p> Response bytes←→≈ 0.39 s08 Oct0.45 s15 Oct1.12 s16 Oct0.97 s16 Oct1.77 s16 Oct <p>This query returns five female Nobel laureates from Wikidata across all prize categories, including Economic Sciences, with laureate labels, prize labels, and prize years, ordered from newest to oldest.</p> <pre><code>echo 'PREFIX p: &lt;http://www.wikidata.org/prop/&gt;
PREFIX ps: &lt;http://www.wikidata.org/prop/statement/&gt;
PREFIX pq: &lt;http://www.wikidata.org/prop/qualifier/&gt;
PREFIX wdt: &lt;http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/&gt;
PREFIX wd: &lt;http://www.wikidata.org/entity/&gt;
PREFIX rdfs: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#&gt;

SELECT ?person ?personLabel ?prizeLabel ?year WHERE {
  {
    SELECT DISTINCT ?prize WHERE {
      { ?prize wdt:P279* wd:Q7191 . } # Nobel Prize
      UNION
      { BIND(wd:Q47170 AS ?prize) } # Economic Sciences
    }
  }
  ?person p:P166 [
    ps:P166 ?prize ;
    pq:P585 ?awardDate
  ] ;
    wdt:P21 wd:Q6581072 . # sex or gender: female
  BIND(YEAR(?awardDate) AS ?year)
  ?person rdfs:label ?personLabel .
  FILTER(LANG(?personLabel) = "en")
  ?prize rdfs:label ?prizeLabel .
  FILTER(LANG(?prizeLabel) = "en")
}
ORDER BY DESC(?year) ?person
LIMIT 5' |
  vitrify sparql \
  --endpoint https://qlever.dev/api/wikidata \
  --query - \
  --format csv \
  --to female-persons
</code></pre> <p> <code>female-persons/</code> ├──  <code>results.csv</code> ├──  <code>ro-crate-metadata.json</code> └──  <code>query.rq</code> </p> <p></p> <p></p> <p></p> results.csvro-crate-metadata.jsonquery.rq <p> personpersonLabelprizeLabelyear http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2633699Anne CarsonNobel Prize in Literature2026 http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q114564137Mary E. BrunkowNobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine2025 http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q439564María Corina MachadoNobel Peace Prize2025 http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q5646626Han KangNobel Prize in Literature2024 http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1097475Claudia GoldinPrize in Economic Sciences in Memory of Alfred Nobel2023 </p> <p>Download <code>results.csv</code></p> <p> <code>results.csv</code></p> <pre><code>{
