WDQSQLever <p>16 Oct 2026, 10:06:57 UTC·Success·0.37 s·76 bytes</p> Response bytes←→≈ 0.31 s10 Oct0.39 s15 Oct0.69 s16 Oct0.44 s16 Oct0.37 s16 Oct <p>With Vitrify installed, run this command in the directory where you want to save <code>fourth-order-classes/</code>:</p> <pre><code>echo 'PREFIX wd: &lt;http://www.wikidata.org/entity/&gt;
PREFIX wdt: &lt;http://www.wikidata.org/prop/direct/&gt;
PREFIX rdfs: &lt;http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#&gt;

SELECT DISTINCT ?class ?classLabel WHERE {
  ?class wdt:P31/wdt:P279* wd:Q24027474 .
  OPTIONAL {
    ?class rdfs:label ?englishLabel .
    FILTER(LANG(?englishLabel) = "en")
  }
  BIND(COALESCE(?englishLabel, STRAFTER(STR(?class), "entity/")) AS ?classLabel)
}
ORDER BY ?classLabel ?class' |
  vitrify sparql \
  --endpoint https://qlever.dev/api/wikidata \
  --query - \
  --format csv \
  --to fourth-order-classes
</code></pre> <p>The query lists all items in Wikidata whose recorded <code>instance of</code> (P31) type is fourth-order class or a subclass of that type, ordered by English label and item URI. A fourth-order class has third-order classes as its instances. This query selects recorded types; it does not check the order of every instance.</p> <p> <code>fourth-order-classes/</code> ├──  <code>results.csv</code> ├──  <code>ro-crate-metadata.json</code> └──  <code>query.rq</code> </p> <p></p> <p></p> <p></p> results.csvro-crate-metadata.jsonquery.rq <p> classclassLabel http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q24017465third-order class </p> <p>Download <code>results.csv</code></p> <p> <code>results.csv</code></p> <pre><code>{
